'''Laksa''' ([[Jawi script|Jawi]]: {{Script/Arabic|لقسا}};<ref>{{cite web |url= https://prpm.dbp.gov.my/cari1?keyword=laksa|title= Carian Umum - Laksa |last= |first= |date= |website= Pusat Rujukan Persuratan Melayu - PRPM|publisher= Dewan Bahasa dan Pustaka - DBP|access-date= 12 Oct 2025}}</ref> [[Chinese language|Chinese]]: 叻沙) is a spicy [[noodle]] dish popular in [[Southeast Asia]].<ref name="SBS-Laksa">{{cite web | author = Siobhan Hegarty | date = 6 February 2017 | title = Think you know laksa? Think again. | work = SBS | url = https://www.sbs.com.au/food/article/2017/02/01/think-you-know-laksa-think-again?cx_navSource=related-side-cx#cxrecs_s}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |url=http://www.meemalee.com/2011/05/laksa-lemak-malaysia-gordons-great.html |title=Laksa Lemak Recipe – Malaysia (Gordon's Great Escape) |date=23 May 2011 |access-date=13 July 2014 |archive-date=26 December 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181226023438/http://www.meemalee.com/2011/05/laksa-lemak-malaysia-gordons-great.html%20 |url-status=live }}</ref> Laksa consists of various types of noodles, most commonly thick rice noodles, with toppings such as [[Chicken as food|chicken]], prawns or fish. Most variations of laksa are prepared with a rich and spicy coconut curry soup or a broth seasoned with a souring ingredient like [[tamarind]] or {{lang|ms|[[Garcinia atroviridis|asam gelugur]]}}.

Originating from [[Peranakan cuisine|Peranakan Chinese cuisine]],<ref name="Nugroho-Laksa"/> laksa recipes are commonly served in [[Singapore]],<ref name="SG Laksa">{{cite web | work = STB | publisher = Singapore Tourism Board | date = 19 September 2019 | title = Singapore Laksa: A local favourite | url = https://www.visitsingapore.com/dining-drinks-singapore/local-dishes/laksa/ | access-date = 19 September 2019 | archive-date = 11 August 2020 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20200811101301/https://www.visitsingapore.com/dining-drinks-singapore/local-dishes/laksa/ | url-status = live }}</ref> [[Indonesia]],<ref name="6 Laksa Indonesia">{{cite web | title = 6 LAKSA Khas Indonesia Paling ENAK Yang Harus Kamu Coba! | author = Ricky Halim | date = 5 August 2015 | work = Qraved | url = https://www.qraved.com/journal/restaurants/6-laksa-khas-indonesia-paling-enak-yang-harus-kamu-coba/ | language = id | access-date = 2 March 2017 | archive-date = 3 March 2017 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20170303042533/https://www.qraved.com/journal/restaurants/6-laksa-khas-indonesia-paling-enak-yang-harus-kamu-coba/ | url-status = live }}</ref> and [[Malaysia]].<ref>{{cite book|last=Siong|first=T.E.|title=Malaysian Diet: The Plain Truth (UM Press)|publisher=The University of Malaya Press|isbn=978-983-100-956-7|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=4xSCDwAAQBAJ&pg=PA4|access-date=10 December 2024|page=4}}</ref>
